    "updated_at": "2019-06-24T13:45:43Z",
    "body": "Checking a random selection of operating systems it does not appear that either Android or Windows support Bluetooth Mesh, which means that it will be difficult for browsers to implement support for it if it were specified by Web Bluetooth.\r\n\r\nExample code for these operating systems utilize the GATT portions of the Bluetooth Mesh specification (provisioning and proxy nodes) and these services should be accessible with Web Bluetooth without changes to the specification.\r\n\r\nLeaving this issue open to track future support for Bluetooth Mesh's other transport layers as support begins to appear in operating systems.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
